+# Implementation Summary: Extended Click Choice Type
+
+## Overview
+Extended the Click `Choice` parameter type to support typed choices (Enum, integers, etc.) consistently across parsing, help display, defaults, and shell completion.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. `src/click/types.py` - Choice Class Enhancement
+
+#### Key Changes:
+- **Import `enum` module** for enum support
+- **Updated `__init__`**: Now accepts `t.Union[t.Sequence[t.Any], t.Type[enum.Enum]]` and consumes iterables once during construction
+- **Added `_get_canonical_token()`**: Returns `.name` for enum members, `str(choice)` otherwise
+- **Added public `normalize_choice()`**: Applies canonical token → ctx.token_normalize_func → casefold (in order)
+- **Updated `convert()`**: 
+  - Uses `normalize_choice()` for comparison
+  - Returns original objects (not string representations)
+  - First match wins when multiple choices normalize to same token
+  - Proper error handling (BadParameter, not AttributeError/TypeError)
+- **Updated `get_metavar()`**: Uses canonical tokens
+- **Updated `get_missing_message()`**: Uses canonical tokens
+- **Updated `shell_complete()`**: 
+  - Uses normalized prefix matching
+  - Returns unnormalized canonical tokens
+  - Deduplicates identical canonical tokens
+  - Offers all distinct tokens that normalize alike
+
+### 2. `src/click/core.py` - Option Help Display
+
+#### Changes to `Option.get_help_record()`:
+- Added special handling for `types.Choice` defaults
+- Displays enum member canonical tokens (not values)
+- Handles list/tuple of enum defaults with comma-space separation
+
+### 3. Test Files Added
+
+#### `tests/test_typed_choice.py` (31 tests)
+Comprehensive tests for all new functionality:
+- Enum choice conversion (basic, str/int subclasses)
+- Integer and other typed choices
+- Case-insensitive Unicode handling
+- Context normalizer support
+- Metavar and help message display
+- Shell completion
+- Multiple/nargs support
+- Environment variables and defaults
+- Reusability across contexts
+
+#### `tests/test_problem_requirements.py` (33 tests)
+Tests matching exact requirements from problem.txt:
+- All 4 examples from requirements
+- All 8 requirement categories
+- Backward compatibility verification
+
+## Features Implemented
+
+### 1. Finite Iterable Support
+✅ Accepts any iterable including one-shot generators  
+✅ Consumes once during construction  
+✅ Preserves original objects  
+✅ Enum classes follow standard Python iteration (excludes aliases)
+
+### 2. Canonical Tokens & Normalization
+✅ `.name` for enum.Enum members (including str/int subclasses)  
+✅ `str(choice)` for non-enum  
+✅ Public `normalize_choice(choice, ctx)` method  
+✅ Order: canonical token → token_normalize_func → casefold  
+✅ Subclasses can override
+
+### 3. Conversion
+✅ Returns original stored objects  
+✅ First match wins with multiple normalizing to same token  
+✅ Works with unhashable choices  
+✅ Raises BadParameter on no match  
+✅ Handles typed defaults (non-string input values)
+
+### 4. Integration
+✅ Works with options and arguments  
+✅ Explicit command-line values  
+✅ Environment variables  
+✅ default_map values  
+✅ Direct and callable defaults  
+✅ multiple=True  
+✅ nargs=N  
+✅ Preserves tuple structure, precedence, callbacks, ParameterSource
+
+### 5. Display
+✅ Metavars use canonical tokens with bracket/brace conventions  
+✅ Missing-value choice lists use canonical tokens  
+✅ Error messages use canonical tokens  
+✅ Enum member names (not qualified names or .value)  
+✅ Compatible method signatures (except new normalize_choice)  
+✅ to_info_dict() exposes original objects
+
+### 6. Help Display
+✅ Enum defaults show canonical tokens  
+✅ List/tuple enum defaults show comma-space separated tokens  
+✅ Preserves explicit show_default overrides  
+✅ Dynamic defaults still show "(dynamic)"
+
+### 7. Shell Completion
+✅ Normalized prefix matching  
+✅ Returns unnormalized canonical tokens  
+✅ Applies to empty input  
+✅ Deduplicates identical canonical tokens  
+✅ Offers all distinct tokens that normalize alike  
+✅ Agreement between conversion and completion on normalization
+
+### 8. Backward Compatibility
+✅ Existing string choice behavior unchanged  
+✅ All 659 existing tests pass  
+✅ No new runtime dependencies  
+✅ No existing assertions weakened or deleted
+
+## Examples Working
+
+```python
+class Mode(Enum):
+    FAST = "fast-value"
+    SAFE = "safe-value"
+
+# Example 1: Enum conversion
+Choice(Mode).convert("FAST", None, None)  # → Mode.FAST
+# Help shows: [FAST|SAFE]
+
+# Example 2: Integer choices
+Choice([10, 20]).convert("20", None, None)  # → 20 (int)
+
+# Example 3: Case-insensitive Unicode
+Choice(["Straße", "STRASSE"], case_sensitive=False).convert("strasse", None, None)  # → "Straße"
+# Completion "STRASS" → ["Straße", "STRASSE"]
+
+# Example 4: Context normalizer
+ctx = Context(..., token_normalize_func=lambda x: x.replace("-", "_"))
+Choice(["read_only"]).convert("read-only", None, ctx)  # → "read_only"
+```
+
